Heeler: route ZeroTier managed routes through a gateway on the network.

libzt never installs a network's managed routes in lwIP: syncManagedStuff
syncs only addresses, each IPv4 netif gets gateway 127.0.0.1, and IPv4 has no
default netif. A route such as 192.168.77.0/24 via 10.147.20.2 (a LAN behind
a member) is therefore unreachable, and connect() times out.

This patch:
- has NodeService::syncManagedStuff hand the network config's IPv4 routes
  that name an IPv4 gateway to the network's tap
  (VirtualTap::setGatewayRoutes4);
- adds VirtualTap::gatewayFor4, a longest-prefix match over those routes;
- adds two lwIP hooks, declared and enabled in lwipopts.h
  (LWIP_HOOK_IP4_ROUTE_SRC, LWIP_HOOK_ETHARP_GET_GW):
  zts_lwip_hook_ip4_route_src keeps a packet whose source is a ZeroTier
  netif's address on that netif, for a destination on its subnet or
  covered by its own routes (one network's controller cannot route
  another network's traffic, even with a more specific route or subnet);
  when no netif reaches the destination lwIP reports no route as before.
  Without a source (an unbound socket), a gateway route is used only while
  a single IPv4 ZeroTier netif is up. zts_lwip_hook_etharp_get_gw returns
  the chosen netif's gateway, from that netif's longest matching route
  whose gateway is on its subnet, so ARP resolves its MAC instead of
  127.0.0.1.

Both hooks run on lwIP's tcpip thread with the core lock held. Heeler binds
each connection to its network's address (heeler_zt_connect), so the
source hook decides its route. An unbound socket's on-subnet traffic still
matches a netif before the hook runs. IPv6 gateway routes are not handled,
as before. Each changed file carries a "Modified by Heeler contributors"
notice.

Applies to libzt commit a707ea6ae0910efdc1125d04758c411e2e9ea4f9 (src/ only).

